{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux relies on specific patterns to ensure correct ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" behavior, efficient rendering, and safe concurrency. This article explains the reasoning behind these patterns.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The Snapshot Pattern","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"The-Snapshot-Pattern"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send()"},{"text":" copies the observer tree into a local struct, mutates the copy via the reducer, then assigns changed properties back. This happens internally via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State(observer:)"},{"text":" packs, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State.apply(_:to:)"},{"text":" unpacks.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The pattern exists for two reasons:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" equality checking.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":" accessor checks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" and suppresses no-op notifications. Swift’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_modify"},{"type":"text","text":" accessor (used by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout"},{"type":"text","text":") fires notifications unconditionally. The snapshot pattern routes through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Cross-slice observation isolation.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates a separate "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" class for each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" property. A view reading "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.items"},{"type":"text","text":" won’t re-render when only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"type":"text","text":" changes, because they live on different observer objects."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"text":" macro generates the observer class tree and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"text":" conformance automatically. Hand-written conformance is still possible for advanced cases — see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Explicit equality guards ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"if x != state.x { x = state.x }"},{"type":"text","text":") are unnecessary. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" already checks equality on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"text":". Unconditional assignment is safe.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"type":"heading","text":"Dispatch Loop Detection","anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"text":" warns if ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":" is called more than 100 times per debounce interval. This usually means ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"text":" isn’t using the snapshot pattern, causing cascading re-renders that trigger re-dispatches.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Reducer Weight","anchor":"Reducer-Weight","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"text":" and dispatch the result back as an action.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Effect-Threading","text":"Effect Threading","type":"heading","level":2},{"name":"Important","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @concurrent in }"},{"type":"text","text":". Blocking calls ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Process.waitUntilExit()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thread.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"important"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use async alternatives: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"terminationHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" + continuation instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"waitUntilExit()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thread.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":", async file I\/O instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data(contentsOf:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance","roleHeading":"Article"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"kind":"article","sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"id